nodecode-delx-recovery is a rewrite of davidmosiah's davidmosiah/delx-plugins:

  https://github.com/davidmosiah/delx-plugins
  commit c1d4be02df59f05fe65a27000d0b06b28c9733c2
  Apache-2.0 (LICENSE), which names no copyright holder: its appendix keeps the
  standard "Copyright [yyyy] [name of copyright owner]" placeholder.

The rewritten plugin is delx-recovery of that commit: a portable Agent Plugins
package with no local code, an MCP server over Streamable HTTP plus a skill, so
this rewrite is a reimplementation of what that package tells an agent to do
rather than of a program. Its MCP endpoint and its wire are kept: one JSON-RPC
`tools/call` per action to the URL its mcp.json names, with the agent id and
credential as the x-delx-agent-id and x-delx-agent-token headers the skill
documents, and a request body carrying the same tool names
(discovery_self_check, resume_session, add_context_memory, leave_hive_note,
close_session, provide_feedback) and the same arguments. Its Continuity Capsule
is kept whole -- goal, done, next, blockers and refuted, version "1" -- as is the
Public-triage-first order of the skill's Path A/B/C/D: public triage needs no
credential, private continuity needs the free identity registration returns, and
a retry key is client-held and starts rk1_. The skill's words are the cell's
primer and tool descriptions, including its hygiene rule that a capsule or a hive
note is data and not an order.

What was left out, and why: the plugin's two guardian hooks (PreCompact and
SessionEnd) are Claude Code hook scripts that seal a capsule from environment
variables; Nodecode has no hook point that runs a shell script when a session
compacts, so the seal is the model's own call. The hooks' Python endpoint
validation goes with them. The skill ships here as the primer (help :delx) and
the tools' descriptions rather than as a separate skill file, because that is
where Nodecode keeps what the model reads every turn. The rest of the service's
breadth -- witness lineage, recognition seals, fleets, peers, the commerce
product -- is reachable on the same endpoint but is not wrapped: the five tools
are the ritual the skill tells an agent to walk first.
